==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|ML.|en}} {{term|ambidexter|lang=la}}, from {{m|la|ambi-}} + {{m|la|dexter}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|/ambɪˈdɛkstə/|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# Someone who is [[ambidextrous]].
# {{context|1811|lang=en}} A lawyer who takes fees from both plaintiff and defendant.
# {{context|by extension|lang=en}} Someone who is [[two-faced]]; a double-dealer.
#* {{RQ:RBrtn AntmyMlncly}}, New York Review of Books, 2001, p.65:
#*: One takes upon him temperence, holiness&nbsp;[…], whenas indeed he, and he, and he, and the rest are hypocrites, '''ambidexters''', outsides, so many turning pictures, a lion on one side, a lamb on the other.

